      ],
      "acceptable_supporting": [
        "presentational-vs-container"
      ]
    },
    "description": "BillingScreen, AdminAuditScreen, ReportViewer, and ExportButton all need permission checks, tenant context, and an analytics event before they render. The permission policy is changing often, and editing every screen would create inconsistent checks. The application already has base components that accept ordinary props, so we need a reusable enhancer factory that accepts a base component and returns an enhanced component with authorization and tenant values injected. The enhanced component must still forward refs, preserve static members, and remain recognizable in React developer tools. Two enhancers must combine, with authorization receiving the tenant supplied by the other enhancer. Tests need to assert that a restricted base component never renders its protected body and that denied attempts produce one analytics event. Existing base components must remain unaware of the permission service and must work unchanged when the enhancement is not installed.",
    "decision_statement": "Choose a reusable way to inject permission, tenant, and analytics behavior across several existing components without modifying or adding knowledge of those concerns to each base component.",
    "notes": "Higher-order-component fits because the factory wraps base components and injects authorization, tenant, and analytics props with ref forwarding and composition; custom-hook is the function-only alternative and presentational-vs-container supports the split. Fixed alias leakage (composable->combine)."
  },
